mixin () {
  public query func getApiDoc() : async Text {
    "# MATHRUSHREE ENTERPRISES — Catalogue Backend API\n\n## Purpose\n\nThis canister is the backend for the MATHRUSHREE ENTERPRISES product catalogue website. It stores the product catalogue (products, categories, subcategories, brands, collections), serves the public catalogue to anonymous visitors, and lets the business owner manage the catalogue from a secure dashboard. It is a **catalogue**, not a shop: there is no cart, checkout, payment, customer account, wishlist, review or order functionality.\n\n## Authentication and identity\n\n- Public read methods (`listPublishedProducts`, `getPublishedProduct`, `listCategories`, `listBrands`, `listCollections`, `listHomepageSections`, `submitEnquiry`) are callable by anyone, including anonymous callers.\n- Owner-only write methods (`createProduct`, `updateProduct`, `duplicateProduct`, `deleteProduct`, `setPublishState`, `setProductFlag`, `createCategory`, `updateCategory`, `deleteCategory`, `createSubcategory`, `updateSubcategory`, `deleteSubcategory`, `createBrand`, `updateBrand`, `deleteBrand`, `createCollection`, `updateCollection`, `deleteCollection`, `assignProductToCollection`, `removeProductFromCollection`, `reorderProductImages`) require a signed-in caller whose role is `#admin`. A non-admin caller receives `#unauthorized` in the returned `CatalogueError`; the call does not trap.\n- `listAllProducts` is an owner-only read: it returns every product regardless of publish state, including drafts and archived rows. A signed-out or non-owner caller receives `null` (it does not trap and does not reveal whether any products exist).\n- The app's frontend pins an Internet Identity derivation origin, published at `/.well-known/ii-derivation-origin` when available. An agent already holding the user's Internet Identity authorization derives the correct per-app principal against that origin (for example `icp identity link web <name> --app <host>`). Such a delegation acts with the user's full authority in this app until it expires.\n- Registration prerequisite: a direct API caller must register before invoking any role-guarded endpoint, including the guarded `listAllProducts` query. Registration is a one-time call to `_initialize_access_control()` made as a signed-in (non-anonymous) caller; an anonymous call is a no-op that registers nobody. The first signed-in caller to initialize becomes `#admin` (the owner); every later signed-in caller becomes `#user`. A principal that never signed in through the app's own frontend is unregistered even if it belongs to the owner, and a principal derived against a different origin is a different principal than the one the frontend registered. An unregistered signed-in caller is not an admin: every owner-only method traps with `\"User is not registered\"` rather than returning `#unauthorized`, and the guarded `listAllProducts` query traps the same way instead of returning `null`. Only a registered non-admin caller receives `#unauthorized`.\n\n## Units and encodings\n\n- `Id` is a `Nat`; ids are assigned by the backend and are unique within their entity.\n- `Timestamp` is a signed `Int` of nanoseconds from `Time.now()` (UTC).\n- `price` is an optional `Nat` in whole Indian Rupees. When `null`, the product has no published price and the website shows \"Enquire for price\".\n- `PublishState` is `#draft`, `#published` or `#archived`. Only `#published` products are visible to public read methods.\n- `Availability` is `#inStock`, `#outOfStock` or `#madeToOrder`.\n- `ProductImage.blob` and `Brand.logo` are object-storage references (`Storage.ExternalBlob`); upload and retrieval go through the object-storage endpoints, not through these catalogue methods.\n- `CatalogueError` is `#notFound`, `#duplicateSku : Text`, `#invalidInput : Text` or `#unauthorized`.\n\n## Lifecycle and polling\n\n- A product is created in whatever `publishState` the caller supplies; the dashboard creates drafts. `setPublishState` moves a product between `#draft`, `#published` and `#archived`. Draft and archived products are hidden from every public read method immediately.\n- `listPublishedProducts` returns a `ProductPage` with `products`, `total`, `page` and `pageSize`. `page` is zero-based; `pageSize` defaults to 12 when omitted or zero. Poll by incrementing `page` until `page * pageSize >= total`.\n- `listAllProducts` returns the same `ProductPage` shape but over all publish states. Its `ProductFilter.search` matches the product name or SKU (case-insensitive, trimmed); `ProductFilter.publishState` restricts to one state (`null` means every state). `categoryId`, `subcategoryId` and `brandId` are ignored by this read. It is a `query` call and returns `null` for a non-owner caller.\n- `listHomepageSections` returns the curated homepage sections (`trending`, `newArrivals`, `bestsellers`, `featured`, `featuredCollections`); a product appears in a section only when it is `#published`, has `showOnHomepage = true`, and carries the matching flag.\n- All changes are persisted immediately and appear on the public website without redeployment.\n\n## Mutation retry safety\n\n- `createProduct` and `createCategory`/`createBrand`/`createCollection` assign a fresh id on every call, so retrying a create after an ambiguous failure can produce a duplicate record. `createProduct` rejects a duplicate SKU with `#duplicateSku`; the other creates do not deduplicate by name.\n- `updateProduct`, `updateCategory`, `updateBrand`, `updateCollection`, `setPublishState`, `setProductFlag`, `assignProductToCollection`, `removeProductFromCollection` and `reorderProductImages` are idempotent: repeating them with the same arguments leaves the same state.\n- `deleteProduct`, `deleteCategory`, `deleteBrand`, `deleteCollection` and `deleteSubcategory` are destructive and return `#notFound` on a second call. `deleteProduct` also removes the product from every collection.\n- `duplicateProduct` creates a new draft with a derived non-colliding SKU (`-COPY`, `-COPY-2`, …); retrying it creates another copy.\n- `submitEnquiry` records the enquiry and, when the `OWNER_EMAIL` environment variable is set, sends a notification email. A failed email send never fails the call; the enquiry is still recorded and `#ok` is returned.\n\n## Errors, limits and gotchas\n\n- Owner-only methods never trap on authorization; they return `#unauthorized`. They do trap only on internal invariants.\n- `createProduct`/`updateProduct` reject a blank name or SKU with `#invalidInput`, and a SKU already used by another product with `#duplicateSku`. SKU comparison is case-insensitive and trims surrounding spaces.\n- `setProductFlag` accepts the flag names `trending`, `newArrival`, `bestseller`, `featured` and `showOnHomepage`; any other name returns `#invalidInput`.\n- `getPublishedProduct` returns `null` for a missing, draft or archived product — it never reveals unpublished products to the public.\n- `submitEnquiry` validates name, contact and message server-side and returns `#err(message)` with a human-readable reason when invalid.\n- The OQL endpoints `schema()` and `execute(queryJson)` expose the catalogue and enquiries to the Caffeine Data Intelligence agent and to a user's own AI assistant. `products` and `enquiries` are controller-only; `categories`, `brands` and `collections` are public."
  };
};
